{% comment %}
  Cartel hero slideshow — 1:1 with the approved prototype (.herowrap in Home.dc.html).
  Each slide = one block. Image OR video per slide; the video slide advances when it ends.
{% endcomment %}
<cl-hero class="cl">
  <section class="herowrap">
    <div class="hero-c ondark">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign fit = block.settings.image_fit
          assign photo_class = 'hero-photo'
          if fit == 'contain'
            assign photo_class = 'hero-photo hero-photo-prod'
          endif
          assign has_video = false
          if block.settings.video != blank
            assign has_video = true
          endif

          # Only slide 1 is visible on load (the rest are opacity:0 + inert below).
          # Marking all four eager/high made them compete for bandwidth AHEAD of
          # the stylesheets and fonts, so the real LCP image got a fraction of the
          # pipe — the classic way to make your own LCP worse. Slide 1 keeps the
          # priority; the others load lazily as the hero cycles to them.
          assign hero_loading = 'lazy'
          assign hero_priority = 'low'
          if forloop.first
            assign hero_loading = 'eager'
            assign hero_priority = 'high'
          endif

          # Blur-up preview (snippets/cartel-lqip.liquid): the photo, or the video's poster
          # still. Packshot (contain) slides keep their flat #eceae7 plate, which already
          # matches the packshot's own background.
          assign lqip_src = nil
          if fit != 'contain'
            if has_video
              assign lqip_src = block.settings.video.preview_image
            else
              assign lqip_src = block.settings.image
            endif
          endif
        -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Inactive slides are only opacity:0 + pointer-events:none, which stops
          the mouse but not the keyboard: every off-screen slide kept its <h1>
          and both CTAs in the tab order and the accessibility tree (four <h1>s
          and six invisible tab stops on the live homepage). `inert` removes
          both; cartel-home.js keeps it in sync as slides change.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div
          class="hero-slide{% if forloop.first %} on{% endif %}{% if fit == 'contain' %} hero-slide--prod{% endif %}"
          {% unless forloop.first %}inert aria-hidden="true"{% endunless %}
          {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
        >
          <div class="hero-media
            {%- if has_video %} hero-media-vid{% endif -%}
            {%- if fit == 'contain' %} hero-media-prod{% endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.image == blank and has_video == false %} hero-media--empty{% endif -%}
            {%- if lqip_src %} lqip{% endif -%}
          "{% if lqip_src %} style="{% render 'cartel-lqip', image: lqip_src %}"{% endif %}>
            {%- if has_video -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                A poster attribute is fetched the moment the parser sees it and cannot be
                lazy-loaded, so every later slide's poster (1600w, ~80KB) downloaded at
                Medium priority next to the LCP image even though the slide is opacity:0.
                Only slide 1 keeps it; cartel-home.js copies data-poster back (data-poster-sm
                on phones) when a slide is shown and warms the next one after window load.
                Built by hand because video_tag emits only the top MP4 rendition: phones
                (the hero's 760px breakpoint) get the smallest rendition that is still
                720p+, about 0.6MB less than the 1080p file every time the slide plays.
                shortcut: a video with no MP4 rendition renders poster-only; Shopify
                transcodes every upload to MP4, so add a video_tag fallback only if one shows up.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign vid = block.settings.video
                assign mp4s = vid.sources | where: 'format', 'mp4' | sort: 'height'
                assign vid_full = mp4s | last
                assign vid_phone = nil
                for src in mp4s
                  if src.height >= 720 and src.height < vid_full.height
                    assign vid_phone = src
                    break
                  endif
                endfor
              -%}
              <video
                class="{{ photo_class }}"
                playsinline
                muted
                preload="none"
                {%- if vid.preview_image %}
                  {%- if forloop.first %}
                    poster="{{ vid.preview_image | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
                  {%- else %}
                    data-poster="{{ vid.preview_image | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
                    data-poster-sm="{{ vid.preview_image | image_url: width: 1100 }}"
                  {%- endif %}
                {%- endif %}
              >
                {%- if vid_phone -%}
                  <source media="(max-width: 760px)" src="{{ vid_phone.url }}" type="{{ vid_phone.mime_type }}">
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if vid_full -%}
                  <source src="{{ vid_full.url }}" type="{{ vid_full.mime_type }}">
                {%- endif -%}
              </video>
            {%- elsif block.settings.image != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                `sizes: '100vw'` was a lie: .herowrap is max-width:1280px with
                40px of padding (cartel-home.css .herowrap), so the image slot is
                never wider than 1200px — every viewport was told to pick a
                candidate a full step or two too large. The padding sits inside
                the max-width (border-box), so the slot is 1200px from a 1280px
                viewport up; the 12px gutters start at the 760px breakpoint.
                1200 is in the ladder because a DPR-1 desktop lands exactly there
                (PSI desktop pulled 1600w for a 1200x679 slot without it); 2400
                stays because a DPR-2 desktop genuinely lands there.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                preload: slide 1 is the LCP element; this puts it in the response's Link
                header (with imagesrcset/imagesizes) so the fetch starts with the document
                instead of after ~110KB of <head>. alt: the photo sits behind the h1 and
                adds nothing the heading doesn't say, so with no alt set in Files it is
                decorative (alt="") — image_tag drops the attribute entirely for a blank
                value, which failed image-alt in both a11y and SEO.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- capture hero_img -%}
                {{
                  block.settings.image
                  | image_url: width: 2400
                  | image_tag:
                    class: photo_class,
                    widths: '760,1100,1200,1600,2000,2400',
                    sizes: '(min-width: 1280px) 1200px, (min-width: 761px) calc(100vw - 80px), calc(100vw - 24px)',
                    loading: hero_loading,
                    fetchpriority: hero_priority,
                    preload: forloop.first,
                    alt: block.settings.image.alt
                }}
              {%- endcapture -%}
              {%- unless hero_img contains ' alt=' -%}
                {%- assign hero_img = hero_img | replace: '<img ', '<img alt="" ' -%}
              {%- endunless -%}
              {{- hero_img -}}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <div class="hero-ov"></div>
          <div class="hero-txt">
            {%- if block.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
              <span class="hero-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>{{ block.settings.eyebrow }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%} h2: the header logo is the homepage H1 (SEO audit 2026-11-18). {%- endcomment -%}
              <h2 class="h-hero">
                {{- block.settings.heading | strip -}}
                {%- if block.settings.heading_accent != blank %} <span class="hero-accent">{{ block.settings.heading_accent }}</span>{% endif -%}
              </h2>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if block.settings.sub != blank -%}<p class="hero-sub">{{ block.settings.sub }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            <div class="hero-cta">
              {%- if block.settings.btn1_label != blank -%}
                <a class="btn btn-bronze" href="{{ block.settings.btn1_link | default: '/collections/all' }}">
                  {{- block.settings.btn1_label -}}
                </a>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if block.settings.btn2_label != blank -%}
                <a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="{{ block.settings.btn2_link | default: '/collections/all' }}">
                  {{- block.settings.btn2_label -}}
                  <svg class="ic-sm" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
                </a>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if section.blocks.size > 1 -%}
        <div class="hero-dots">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            <button
              class="hero-dot{% if forloop.first %} on{% endif %}"
              type="button"
              data-hero-dot
              aria-label="Show slide {{ forloop.index }}"
            >
              <span class="hero-fill"></span>
            </button>
          {%- endfor -%}
          <button class="hero-play" type="button" data-hero-play aria-label="Pause slideshow">
            <svg class="ic-xs" data-icon-pause viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6.5" y="5" width="3.6" height="14" rx="1.2"></rect><rect x="13.9" y="5" width="3.6" height="14" rx="1.2"></rect></svg>
            <svg class="ic-xs" data-icon-play viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 4.5v15l12-7.5z"></path></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </section>
</cl-hero>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cartel hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "cartel-section",
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Each slide holds an image or a video. Upload web-optimised MP4s (faststart) so the video slide starts instantly."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "slide",
      "name": "Slide",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
        { "type": "video", "id": "video", "label": "Video (overrides image)" },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "image_fit",
          "label": "Media fit",
          "options": [
            { "value": "cover", "label": "Fill the frame (photos)" },
            { "value": "contain", "label": "Show the whole product (packshots)" }
          ],
          "default": "cover"
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "New season · 2026" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Stock your kit like a " },
        { "type": "text", "id": "heading_accent", "label": "Heading accent (bronze)", "default": "pro." },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "sub",
          "label": "Subheading",
          "default": "Pro-grade adhesives, Korean lash lift, brow lamination and tints, curated for Canadian artists, shipped fast and 100% authentic."
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "btn1_label", "label": "Primary button", "default": "Shop the collection" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "btn1_link", "label": "Primary link" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "btn2_label", "label": "Secondary button", "default": "Explore lash lift" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "btn2_link", "label": "Secondary link" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Cartel hero",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "slide" }, { "type": "slide" }, { "type": "slide" }, { "type": "slide" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
